's prompt is unsound.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda6f57b9cf188fdf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > 'The marker record, and where its interpretation protocol lives'; Scope > 'T1's prompt and its suppress_types are out of scope deliberately'","norm_id":"n6fee16b03c4ebc56","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A backend raises DDGSException('timeout'); the marker is returned; T1 sees a search-result-shaped record whose body says 'do not conclude none exists'; per its prompt T1 treats that text as untrusted data to report on, not a rule to apply, and may still conclude prior art was checked."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Bring T1's prompt into scope for a minimal, coordinated edit: add a clause recognizing a title==WEB_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE record as a rebar-issued tool-failure notice (not third-party data) whose body IS to be applied, so co-location has an effective reader-side anchor.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite the pydantic-ai seam that accepts the rebar wrapper (duckduckgo_search_tool's client parameter signature, or the type WebSearch.local accepts) and state which layer the DDGSException catch sits at, classifying it Verified rather than Partially-verified.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4176,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Verified via resolve_symbol: DDGSException, DuckDuckGoResult, duckduckgo_search_tool, WebSearch all EXIST in the installed environment.","capabilities.py:157 currently passes local=duckduckgo_search_tool(max_results=...), i.e. local= receives the tool object that duckduckgo_search_tool builds around the client.","The plan says 'wrapping the client' and 'installs rebar's wrapper as the local tool, not pydantic-ai's raw duckduckgo_search_tool' (AC4) — two different seams (client-layer vs tool-object-layer) that the plan does not disambiguate with a cited signature.","Evidence class: Partially-verified — the integration exists and symbols are real, but the specific seam accepting the rebar wrapper is unconfirmed."],"finding":"The wrapping seam the plan depends on is only partially verified: it asserts WebSearch(local=...) will accept a rebar-owned callable wrapping the ddgs client, but does not cite the signature of duckduckgo_search_tool / the shape local= requires, so it is unconfirmed whether the wrapper is installed at the client layer (passed into duckduckgo_search_tool) or as a replacement tool object at local=.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f42b0cef60b270730","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (decided) — 'builds a rebar-owned local search callable wrapping the client'; capabilities.py:150-158","norm_id":"n3aac0f83171a2606","priority":0.4824,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If duckduckgo_search_tool does not accept a custom client and local= only accepts its returned tool object, the wrapper must intercept at a 