efinition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a log line (and/or metric) at the wrapper's DDGSException catch recording the branch and backend message, so branch-1 degradations are visible to operators, and add an AC asserting the log is emitted.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan catches ddgs.exceptions.DDGSException at the boundary but never mentions logging, a metric, or a trace on catch","Branch 1 'return an empty list' is by the plan's own admission indistinguishable from a true-empty search, so the failure signal is lost with no operator-facing record","Eight tickets were caused by this defect, yet nothing in the plan lets an operator see the wrapper is now silently degrading"],"finding":"The new catch boundary emits no log/metric, so a caught DDGSException — especially branch 1 where a real backend failure returning \"No results found.\" is converted to an empty list indistinguishable from a genuine empty result — is operationally invisible to operators.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f163d9875a0ad6b18","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'Behaviour on catch' (branches 1 and 2)","norm_id":"n02406aaa8007a3bd","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A backend outage that yields 'No results found.' silently degrades every future T1 with no way to notice the search is failing rather than genuinely finding nothing"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the wrapper's except block, log a WARNING including the caught message before returning empty/marker, and add an AC that asserts the log record is emitted on catch (via caplog) for both branches.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how branch 1's exact-string discriminator survives a ddgs default-message change: pin ddgs to a version whose 'No results found.' text is asserted, add a test that fails if the upstream default drifts, and/or note in the plan that a drift degrades toward the marker (fail-safe) as accepted behaviour.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Message exactly \"No results found.\" - indistinguishable ... so return an empty list.'","Plan root-cause: 'ddgs/ddgs.py:454 does raise DDGSException(err or \"No results found.\")' — the string is a library default, not a rebar constant","pyproject.toml:133: 'pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries,duckduckgo]>=1.107,<2' — ddgs is transitive, not directly pinned, so the default message can change within the allowed range"],"finding":"Branch 1 keys on an exact match of the string 'No results found.', which is only a hardcoded DEFAULT inside the transitively-resolved ddgs library (ddgs.py:454: raise DDGSException(err or 'No results found.')); rebar does not pin ddgs directly (it floats within pydantic-ai-slim[...duckduckgo]>=1.107,<2), so if that default text drifts across versions the branch-1 discriminator silently stops matching.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f489057596b92227a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (decided) -> 'Behaviour on catch', branch 1; AC1","norm_id":"nb6de09b11f57bde4","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ddgs (or pydantic-ai's dependency on it) upgrades and changes the zero-result default wording; every genuinely-empty prior-art search now falls into branch 2 and emits a WEB_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE marker instead of completing clean"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a note (and a guard test) tying branch 1 to the observed ddgs default string, so an upstream wording change is caught by CI rather than silently converting empty results into markers; alternatively document explicitly that string drift is an accepted fail-safe degradation toward branch 2.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how T1 should treat a zero-result prior-art search (empty list) so a backend failure masquerading as 'No results found.' does not become a silent 'no prior art exists' conclusion.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: branch 1 'Message exactly \"No results found.\" - indistinguishable between true-empty and backend-failed, so return an empty list. T1 reasons from no prior-art results were returned and the review COMPLETES.'","T1 checklist keys 'prior_art' and 'capability_assertions_resolved' (criteria_routing.json:589-599) give T1 no protocol for distinguishing a real empty result from a swallowed backend failure.","The plan's own trap section: 'a handler that swallows the exception and returns [] ... would make T1 conclude no prior art exists when the search actually failed.'"],"finding":"Branch 1 (empty list) has no specified reader-side fallback: an empty result is indistinguishable to T1 from a genuinely-empty search, so when a backend actually failed T1 will silently conclude 'no prior art exists' — the same quiet-wrong-answer the plan says it is avoiding, just moved from the boundary into T1's reasoning.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5fed33061579e76c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Behaviour on catch, item 1; AC1","norm_id":"n0566d789a1fa69bc","priority":0.2513,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["All backends fail with the common 'No results found.' message on a real bright-line plan; branch 1 returns []; T1 concludes prior art was checked and none exists; a MAJOR prior-art finding i